---
/**
 * /development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology — the landing for the draft ontology extracted from PDTF schema and
 * its woven technical reference (ADR-0041).
 *
 * The combination principle: the /development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology section is one woven reference made
 * of off-the-shelf tool renderings (where they win), custom opda-gen scripts
 * (for the OPDA-specific layers), and LLM-authored prose (the conceptual layer).
 * This page is the entry point: what the section is, the live headline counts,
 * and a card grid into every page of the section.
 *
 * The bake-off tools catalogue + M6 scorecard + embeds now live on
 * /ontology/bake-off. Counts are computed at build time (read-only) from the
 * committed TTL corpus at source/03-standards/ontology/.
 */
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';

const ONT = path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'source/03-standards/ontology');

/** Read a TTL file, returning '' if missing (corpus is edited concurrently). */
function ttl(name: string): string {
  try { return fs.readFileSync(path.join(ONT, name), 'utf8'); } catch { return ''; }
}
/** Count regex matches across a set of module TTLs. */
function countAcross(files: string[], re: RegExp): number {
  let n = 0;
  for (const f of files) { const m = ttl(f).match(re); if (m) n += m.length; }
  return n;
}
function countDir(rel: string, suffix: string, exclude?: string): number {
  try {
    return fs.readdirSync(path.join(ONT, rel))
      .filter((f) => f.endsWith(suffix) && (!exclude || !f.includes(exclude))).length;
  } catch { return 0; }
}

const MODULES = ['opda-classes.ttl', 'opda-property.ttl', 'opda-agent.ttl',
  'opda-transaction.ttl', 'opda-claim.ttl', 'opda-governance.ttl',
  'opda-descriptive.ttl', 'foundation.ttl'];
const SHAPES = ['opda-shapes.ttl', 'opda-property-shapes.ttl', 'opda-agent-shapes.ttl',
  'opda-transaction-shapes.ttl', 'opda-claim-shapes.ttl', 'opda-governance-shapes.ttl',
  'opda-descriptive-shapes.ttl'];

// LIVE counts from the committed corpus (rdf:type form).
const counts = {
  classes:     countAcross(MODULES, /rdf:type owl:Class/g),
  objectProps: countAcross(MODULES, /rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty/g),
  dataProps:   countAcross(MODULES, /rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty/g),
  schemes:     countAcross(['opda-vocabularies.ttl'], /rdf:type skos:ConceptScheme/g),
  concepts:    countAcross(['opda-vocabularies.ttl'], /rdf:type skos:Concept\b/g),
  shapes:      countAcross(SHAPES, /sh:NodeShape/g),
  profiles:    countDir('profiles', '.ttl'),
  exemplars:   countDir('exemplars', '.ttl', 'expected-report'),
};
---
<Layout
  title="Schema-derived ontology"
  description="The draft, schema-derived ontology reference generated from the committed TTL corpus; it is not the approved SPDTF model."
>
  <h1>Schema-derived ontology reference</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    This is a draft semantic artefact derived from the PDTF schema, its dictionaries,
    documents and recorded decisions. Everything here is generated from the committed
    TTL corpus at <code>source/03-standards/ontology/</code> and guarded by the doc-drift
    CI gate. Reproducible generation makes it a canonical reference for that committed
    corpus; it does not make the draft an approved standard or the SPDTF ontology.
  </p>
  <p>SPDTF reuses this corpus as attributed evidence. Start with <a href="/semantic-modelling/why-ontologies">why ontologies</a> and the current domain-led method.</p>
  <p>
    This ontology is separate from the <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema">PDTF schema</a>. The
    <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/schema">JSON Schema package</a>,
    dictionary, glossary and related evidence are its attributed sources; the ontology
    remains a separately status-labelled draft and is not an endorsed scheme.
    The <a href="/development/property-pack/pdtf-schema-lineage">Property Pack lineage</a>
    records what is proven and what still needs a semantic crosswalk.
  </p>


  <h2 id="combination">The combination principle</h2>
  <p>
    No single off-the-shelf tool documents the whole ontology — the OWL generators skip SHACL
    and treat SKOS unevenly, and none render the OPDA-specific layers at all. So this reference
    is one <strong>woven composition</strong> of three methods (<a href="/modelling/adr/adr-0041">ADR-0041</a>):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Tool renderings</strong> — the best off-the-shelf tool per layer (pyLODE / WIDOCO for OWL, SHACL Play! for shapes, Ontospy / Skosmos for SKOS), scored in the <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/use-and-tooling/bake-off">bake-off</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Custom <code>opda-gen</code> scripts</strong> — the OPDA-specific layers no tool covers: the overlay profiles + GAP register, the round-trip exemplars, and the three-graph separation.</li>
    <li><strong>LLM-authored prose</strong> — the conceptual / governance layer a generator cannot emit: <em>why</em> the model is shaped as it is, the decision provenance, and the known-issues register.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Redundancy with neighbouring sections is intended and fine (<a href="/modelling/adr/adr-0041">ADR-0041</a> rev-3, M1) — this
    section is designed standalone. For <em>how</em> the model was built see
    <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification/historical-modelling">Modelling</a>; for the DAMA four-tier reader presentation see
    <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/model-views-by-audience">Model</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <div class="callout__label">Status — draft, under review</div>
    <p>
      The PDTF-to-ontology programme is <strong>RETIRED 2026-06-14</strong> (a historical
      anchor; modelling continues under fresh ODRs). This reference carries
      <code>status: draft</code> until the doc-drift CI gate is green and the operator settles
      the per-layer pick (<a href="/modelling/adr/adr-0041">ADR-0041</a> M6). See <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification/decision-provenance">Decision
      provenance</a> for the full retirement and ratification record.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="counts">Live headline counts</h2>
  <p>
    Read at build time from the committed TTL corpus — these numbers cannot drift from the
    model without failing the doc-drift gate.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Live count</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>OWL classes</td><td>{counts.classes}</td><td>module TTLs (asserted <code>owl:Class</code>)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Object properties</td><td>{counts.objectProps}</td><td><code>owl:ObjectProperty</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Datatype properties</td><td>{counts.dataProps}</td><td><code>owl:DatatypeProperty</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>SKOS concept schemes</td><td>{counts.schemes}</td><td><code>opda-vocabularies.ttl</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>SKOS concepts</td><td>{counts.concepts}</td><td><code>opda-vocabularies.ttl</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>SHACL base node-shapes</td><td>{counts.shapes}</td><td><code>*-shapes.ttl</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Overlay profiles</td><td>{counts.profiles}</td><td><code>profiles/*.ttl</code> (most thin by design)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Round-trip exemplars</td><td>{counts.exemplars}</td><td><code>exemplars/*.ttl</code> (scenario inputs)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="muted tiny">
    Profiles are mostly <strong>thin by design</strong> — they bind Category-G leaves only, and
    GAP-register the rest (224 bound / 1095 GAPped at session-034). See
    <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/trust-governance-and-limitations/known-issues#thin">Known issues</a> for why that is the ratified outcome,
    not an omission. Downloadable TTL bundles are on <a href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/use-and-tooling/usage#downloads">Consume
    the ontology</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="explore">Explore the reference</h2>
  <p>
    Choose the task that brought you here. Each category page explains its scope and
    authority boundary before linking to the detailed generated and hand-authored views.
  </p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification" title="Lineage, provenance and verification" eyebrow="Trace and check" description="Follow sources and decisions, review the historical modelling record, and inspect the independent RML schema–ontology verification bridge." />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/model-views-by-audience" title="Model views by audience" eyebrow="Choose a view" description="Move from information architecture through concept and logical views to ontology, deployment and relational implementations." />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/concepts-and-architecture" title="Concepts and architecture" eyebrow="Understand the model" description="Study identity, classification, context modules, foundational commitments and the bounded use of modelling frameworks." />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/terms-and-model-resources" title="Terms and model resources" eyebrow="Find a resource" description={`Browse the graph, ${counts.classes} classes, ${counts.objectProps + counts.dataProps} properties, datatypes, vocabularies and the A–Z term index.`} />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/validation-and-examples" title="Validation and examples" eyebrow="Test the model" description={`Inspect ${counts.shapes} SHACL node shapes, ${counts.profiles} overlay profiles and ${counts.exemplars} diagnostic exemplars.`} />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/trust-governance-and-limitations" title="Trust, governance and limitations" eyebrow="Interpret authority" description="Separate claims, evidence, PII and semantic governance, then review the limitations and known-issues register." />
    <GatewayCard href="/development/inputs/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology/use-and-tooling" title="Use and tooling" eyebrow="Consume the corpus" description="Bind namespaces, download and query the Turtle corpus, reproduce validation and compare supplementary tool renderings." />
  </div>
</Layout>
